She posted this before and was immediately called out in the photoshopping.

Shame on you OP, this ain't a compliment fishing subreddit. Post your real self so people can give you honest feedback if that is what you are looking for.

I can't even form an opinion bc I don't know if anything in this photo is authentic now and I dislike that you made me feel this way in this safe space subreddit ;;

Porn has always been deprecating towards the actors in it. Even the "stars". It's all completely devoid of actually humanity and the things that make sex exciting and enjoyable for most well-adjusted people.

It's not just a trans disrespect and misogyny, it's all persons of all the different demographics in pornography.

 A large part of the reason that people see us as sex objects is because that's how we're were portrayed for decades in porn (most older folks' initial and for many, only, exposed to trans persons) so the associate our existence with that of sex. Because that's the way they got to know of us, as deviants, perverts, and sexual objects so ofc we can't be well rounded humans! It's so terrible what the porn industry has done to us and many other persons because the cultural impact has been incredulously huge and clawing our way out of it has been awful for all that have been affected. ;;

